-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| `main(String[] args)`                         | `args: String[]`                                                                                                      | `void`                              | Initializes the application, loads services, operates in a menu-driven loop for cheque processing and ancillary tasks.                                    |\n| `performLogin(Scanner scanner, UserService userService)` | `scanner: Scanner`, `userService: UserService`                                                                         | `User`                              | Reads user input for login, authenticates users, and logs failed attempts (up to three).                                                                 |\n| `processChequeBatch(Scanner scanner, ChequeProcessor chequeProcessor)` | `scanner: Scanner`, `chequeProcessor: ChequeProcessor`                                                                | `void`                              | Allows the user to input details for multiple cheques, processes them, and may log errors during processing.                                              |\n| `displayCurrencyExchangeMenu(Scanner scanner, CurrencyExchangeService currencyExchangeService)` | `scanner: Scanner`, `currencyExchangeService: CurrencyExchangeService`                                                | `void`                              | Displays options for watching currency exchange rates or performing conversions and handles repeated user actions.                                        |\n| `handleReportGeneration(Scanner scanner, ChequeHistoryManager chequeHistoryManager)` | `scanner: Scanner`, `chequeHistoryManager: ChequeHistoryManager`                                                      | `void`                              | Generates and exports cheque history reports for specific time periods or custom ranges.                                                                 |\n| `handleChequePrinting(Scanner scanner, ChequePrintingService printingService)` | `scanner: Scanner`, `printingService: ChequePrintingService`                                                          | `void`                              | Simulates cheque printing functionality based on user-provided cheque details.                                                                            |\n| `handleChequeImageSubmission(Scanner scanner, ChequeImageHandler imageHandler, CryptographyService cryptoService, ClearinghouseService clearinghouseService, User currentUser)` | `scanner: Scanner`, `imageHandler: ChequeImageHandler`, `cryptoService: CryptographyService`, `clearinghouseService: ClearinghouseService`, `currentUser: User` | `void`                              | Uploads cheque images, encrypts and signs them, and submits the files to the clearinghouse.                                                               |\n| `processCheque(String accountNumber, String chequeNumber, String currency, double amount, String signature)` | `accountNumber: String`, `chequeNumber: String`, `currency: String`, `amount: double`, `signature: String`             | `void`                              | Processes a single cheque, executing fraud detection, signature verification, and history updates.                                                        |\n| `authenticate(String username, String password)` | `username: String`, `REDACTED                                                                                | `User`                              | Authenticates a user and returns the corresponding `User` object.                                                                                         |\n\n## Business Rules\n\n1. Users must provide valid credentials (username and password) to access the system; maximum of three login attempts is allowed.\n2. Cheques must be processed in batches or individually, with details such as account number, cheque number, currency, and signature.\n3. Currency exchange rates should be fetched from an external API, and rates should be cached for subsequent use to minimize API overhead.\n4. Fraud checks (e.g., duplicate cheque checks and abnormal activity detection) must be conducted on all cheque transactions.\n5. The system must handle exceptions gracefully to ensure continuity of operations (e.g., retrying API calls or logging issues for later review).\n6. Cheque image submissions must be encrypted, signed, and securely transmitted to the clearinghouse.\n7. Cheque statuses (e.g., issued, processed, canceled) must be accurately tracked in the system\'s lifecycle.\n8. Reports and logs must be generated and stored with accurate details for auditing and historical purposes.\n9. All external API errors (e.g., currency exchange API fetch failures) must be managed with retry mechanisms or fallback procedures.\n\n## Data Structures\n\n### Class: `DemoApplication`\n\n| **Field Name** | **Type** | **Description** |\n|----------------|----------|-----------------|\n| *(none)*       |          |                 |\n\n### Class: `ChequeApplication`\n\n| **Field Name** | **Type** | **Description** |\n|----------------|----------|-----------------|\n| *(none)*       |          |                 |\n\n### Class: `User`\n\n| **Field Name** | **Type** | **Description**       |\n|----------------|----------|-----------------------|\n| `username`     | `String` | User\'s login username |\n| `password`     | `String` | User\'s password       |\n| `role`         | `String` | User\'s assigned role  |\n\n### Class: `BatchCheque`\n\n| **Field Name**   | **Type**  | **Description**              |\n|------------------|-----------|------------------------------|\n| `accountNumber`  | `String`  | Account number associated with the cheque |\n| `chequeNumber`   | `String`  | Unique cheque number         |\n| `currency`       | `